<% confirm_url = user_confirmation_url(confirmation_token: @token) %>
<h1 style="margin: 0 0 16px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; color: #09090b;">Confirm your email address</h1>

<p style="margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Hello <%= @email %>,</p>

<p style="margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Confirm that this is your address to use it on Makerstorage. Organizations invite members by email, so invitations sent to this address only show up once it&#39;s confirmed.</p>

<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="margin: 24px 0;">
  <tr>
    <td style="border-radius: 8px; background-color: #facc15;">
      <a href="<%= confirm_url %>" style="display: inline-block; padding: 12px 22px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: #1c1917; text-decoration: none;">Confirm email</a>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<p style="margin: 0 0 16px 0; font-size: 13px; color: #71717a;">
  This link expires in <%= (Devise.confirm_within / 86_400).to_i %> days. If the button doesn&#39;t work, copy and paste this URL into your browser:<br>
  <a href="<%= confirm_url %>" style="color: #71717a; word-break: break-all;"><%= confirm_url %></a>
</p>

<p style="margin: 16px 0 0 0;">If you didn&#39;t sign up or change your email on Makerstorage, you can safely ignore this email.</p>
